From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] gtk4: handle zoom keys on focused Home surface

Home owns focus for the default shell view. Route Sugar's semantic zoom keys
from its GTK4 event controller as well as the top-level controller so F1/F2
cannot be consumed by the search widget or focus chain.

--- a/src/jarabe/desktop/homewindow.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/desktop/homewindow.py
@@ -202,6 +202,17 @@
     def __key_pressed_cb(self, controller, keyval, keycode, state):
+        zoom_levels = {
+            Gdk.KEY_F1: ShellModel.ZOOM_MESH,
+            Gdk.KEY_F2: ShellModel.ZOOM_GROUP,
+            Gdk.KEY_F3: ShellModel.ZOOM_HOME,
+            Gdk.KEY_F4: ShellModel.ZOOM_ACTIVITY,
+        }
+        if keyval in zoom_levels:
+            shell.get_model().set_zoom_level(zoom_levels[keyval])
+            return True
+
         if self.__is_alt(keyval, state) and not getattr(self, '_alt_held', False):
